; THE BIG CITY (GAMEPLAY-DESIGN Iteration 16 / L13 phase 0.2, the user's
; "easy/cheap win"). 12 x 15 = 180 blocks, up from 4 x 5 = 20: nine times the
; content and about 550 x 750 m of it, which is the first environment in this
; game you can get lost in.
;
; THE SIZE IS CHOSEN FROM A MEASUREMENT, not from taste. `city_load_bench`
; sweeps this generator from 20 blocks to 400 and the cost is FLAT PER BLOCK
; across the whole range - about 4800 triangles and 30 meshes each, with no
; term that grows faster than the block count. So the ceiling is not structural
; and this number is a budget decision: 180 blocks is 832k triangles, 5373
; meshes and 0.9 s to generate, which leaves room to double again.
[node name="City" type="Node3D" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("7_city")
layout_seed = 42
cols = 12
rows = 15
interiors_enabled = true
block_size = 32.0
road_width = 16.0
front_z = -50.0
min_floors = 10
max_floors = 30
